munity so as Skyrim's  release date approached the community  began to discuss how these large-scale  mods should be handled  while beyond Skyrim wasn't the idea of a  single person or team the website points  to a post started by candle master on  the beth soft forums that ignited the  spark that led to beyond Skyrim rather  than unifying different teams to create  the entirety of Tamriel beyond Skyrim  along with dark creation  a hub for modders was used as a vehicle  to coordinate with different teams share  resources and give all the teams a  single platform to share their creations  with fellow modders and the world apart  from a set of rules and procedures  outlined in the beyond Skyrim  Constitution the only caveat is that  these regions have to be lore friendly  take place around the same time as the  events of Skyrim and the overall quality  must be on par or exceed that of Elder  Scrolls 5 but again the team behind  Serie Dell and Bruma is only one of  seven each of these teams have their own  design philosophies region specific  resources and different stories to tell  rich Marin one of the leads for serie  Dell related it to the Marvel Cinematic  Universe all of these separate mods are  free to tell their own stories but the  developers are aware that these  creations and stories should fit within  the larger universe that beyond Skyrim  has put forth for example one team can't  create a quest line that destroys all of  Tamriel  Maran has been modding for six years now  he began on a project to recreate souls  time a small region northeast of Skyrim  however weeks into the project Bethesda  announced Dragonborn an expansion that  took place in the very same region they  were recreating the project was  shuttered and rich took notice of an  inactive serie del project without a  lead he threw his name in the running  and with some help from Marcus Liberty a  creative who helped with Bruma he got  the position over the years beyond  Skyrim has unified certain aspects of  development such as voice acting and the  music department in fact the music  you're hearing in this video was  composed by Daniel ran for beyond Skyrim  Bruma  [Music]  but a lot of these decisions are left to  the autonomous teams while new ideas  still need to be vetted the cyrodiil  team is open to experimentation even if  it doesn't quite sink up with the lure  and that's one of the many things that's  so cool about this project as messy as  Elder Scrolls lore can get there is so  much room for interpretation and  untapped potential most developers build  off their Laura's new titles release but  these mods have the power to give us a  fresh and vastly different take on areas  that were explored years ago or only  referenced and Bruma alone I can already  see how the team is planting seeds for a  larger plot line and I couldn't be more  excited to see where they take it and I  hear rumors whispers on the wind of  insurrectionist groups agitating against  the current government there are so many  opportunities to explore here take iliac  bay a few weeks ago the team released a  beautiful trailer for their mod and it's  brimming with potential sure we saw high  rock and hammer fell in the elder  scrolls too but never quite like this  seeing lush jungles and deserts is not  only a breath of fresh air but it holds  thousands of new possibilities and  scenarios that we would have never  experienced in Skyrim what Larry and Meg  Lowe Smith team are doing with morrowind  is another perfect example of that in  the official lore morrowind was  devastated by a volcano before the  events of Skyrim things are very  different than what you remember from  the Elder Scrolls 3 and the morrowind  team is embracing that parts of the  world are caked with ash and a smoky  haze hangs over the province the  prospect of this is even more  interesting if you consider the fact  that we may never see what Marlin looked  like after the volcano erupted in any  official capacity the mod is  appropriately titled morrowind the star  wounded east  [Music]  both meg Lowe's and Larry enjoined the  Morrowind team in 2016 after a shift in  direction and reshuffling of leadership  that who found themselves as directors  while they stick to lore whenever  possible they get a lot of inspiration  from the Tamriel rebuilt team the  geography on the other hand is pieced  together from multiple sources once  again the team considers Tamriel rebuilt  as their primary source but many of the  locations from Elder Scrolls online also  appear in their vision of morrowind when  I asked Marin about all these different  directions the mods are going he said  that he thinks it beyond Skyrim as a  huge collection of work for folks who  are trying to break into the industry or  bolster their portfolios in fact Larian  one of the directors on morrowind is  hoping for this to be his foot in the  door once he's done with school  as of now the only beyond Skyrim mod  available is Bruma it adds the Jerell  Mountains in the frigid city of Bruma  with the mod installed you can find a  border crossing on the southern end of  Skyrim after convincing the guards to  let you through you take your first  steps in serie dell having played around  15 hours of this mod the first thing i  noticed was how professional it looks  the voice acting branching narratives  and quests design is as good if not  better at times than anything you'd see  in a Bethesda Game Studios RPG plus it  has its fair share of weird quests which  I personally love yes the nirn theater  the center stage of the imperial city of  the world they cast me out the  irredeemable fools  according to Moran beyond Skyrim Bruma  originally began as a proof-of-concept  the scope was much smaller and the main  focus would be on the city itself after  promising a summer 2014 release date the  team decided that if they did hit that  release window they would have to  drastically cut back on content and the  level of polish wouldn't be up to par  back in July we came to a difficult  decision we were going to delay beyond  Skyrim Bruma we had announced it on our  Facebook page but we decided to announce  it here also to make sure everyone is  aware  it wasn't until 2017 that the mod  finally released and it's clear that all  that extra time went to good use there  were more quests more creatures an  original score and more detail  overall the completed model or like an  overly ambitious expansion than a demo  of what's to come three more years might  sound like a long time but creating  something even of this scale is a  massive endeavor these large-scale mods  begin with a height map a low poly  aerial map of a landmass then for Bruma  at least the assets like buildings  weapons dungeons armor sets and  vegetation are created we are talking  thousands of individually crafted items  even something as simple as the iron  weapons from Skyrim or redesigned for  Bruma after the space has been molded  these assets are added and then quests  characters and storylines are  implemented then you have to consider  voice acting music sound effects bug  testing performance animations interiors  balancing NPC routes  text found in books scattered throughout  the world and so on the point is in  order to create something of this  caliber it requires a lot of time and  their work is starting to really pay off  the Bruma trailer has over 1 million  views on YouTube nearly a million  downloads on Nexus mods and a quarter of  a million downloads on Xbox one and it  sounds like this success is exciting for  the other teams as well according to Meg  lows from the morrowind team Bruma  really put them on the map many more  people became aware of this project and  in turn more people joined the various  teams above all though it proved to them  that what they were trying to achieve  could actually be done  however Marin isn't sure if this success  will continue forever like oblivion and  morrowind before this modders typically  follow the games that will get their  creations the most exposure and fans  typically care more about the latest  iteration well I can't imagine these  mods shutting down when the Elder  Scrolls 6 releases it certainly does  pose a threat the best-case scenario is  that these mods release during Skyrim's  lifecycle fortunately for the modding  teams Bethesda has stated that its next  installment is coming but it's still a  ways out and as Meg Lowe's points out  people have been modding morrowind for  over 15 years the community is still  going strong at most  meg Lewis believes that they will see a  drop in membership when six launches but  production on the mods won't halt  altogether  another common fear for a project like  this is turnover when your team is  entirely composed of volunteers you  think the workforce would come and go  frequently however Marin assured me that  that isn't necessarily the case while he  couldn't speak for the other teams the  core group behind Serie Dell has been  around for three to four years and as of  now sir Adele has roughly 40 to 50  members made up of artists audio  designers writers level designers  animators and so on but even for 50  dedicated people this is still a massive  undertaking morrowind on the other hand  has a larger headcount  however Larian did mention that 3d  artists can be difficult to hold on to  due to Skyrim stated engine 3d artists  have stricter limitations than other  departments  despite the scope of this project marin  Laren and megaliths made it clear that  life comes first as exciting and  demanding as all these projects may be  it shouldn't take priority over school  work well-being or family after all  there is no money involved in any of  these projects most of these volunteers  are trying to do the impossible while  living a life typically when we hear  about mods of this scale they either  never see the light of day or are  forgotten when they finally release it's  tough to keep a project like this going  without a significant amount of money  backing it and even harder when your  developers are largely made up of  volunteers nevertheless these teams push  onward beyond Skyrim feels like a direct  response to the failings and  shortcomings of previous standalone mods  made for Oblivion and morrowind rather  than working entirely  independent of one another that beyond  Skyrim teams have built something that  allows everyone to work toward a similar  goal while blazing their own unique  trails against all odds they are  creating something far bigger than what  the Fez de originally created in 2011  something far bigger than anything we  typically see from triple-a developers  and something that's fulfilling the  dream many never thought was possible  the dream of recreating Tamriel is  slowly becoming a reality so I think a  little patience on our end isn't too  much to ask in an industry where  publishers hide content behind paywalls  and drip feed players in order to keep  them coming back it's refreshing to see  a game that's being kept alive entirely  by the community apart from re-releases  Bethesda stopped updating Skyrim and  adding DLC years ago yet I still find  myself coming back every few months  thanks to folks like Marin Larry and Meg  Lowe's to me Skyrim no longer feels like  that janky immersive RPG Bethesda  created all those years ago  it's an adventure that's constantly  changing beneath my feet and heading in  all sorts of exciting directions I would  have never imagined it's hard to say  whether or not beyond Skyrim will hit  all those lofty goals they've set for  themselves but is someone looking in  from the outside it's clear they have  built up an infrastructure to not only  make a bigger Tamriel possible but  attainable  [Music]  you  you
 

